<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arctic Ocean</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arctic Ocean is the smallest and shallowest of the world's oceans, surrounding the North Pole and bordered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>. Much of it is covered by sea ice for most of the year. Between 1920 and 1944 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> reached it through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petsamo">Petsamo</a> corridor, and its northern sea routes have grown in strategic and economic importance as the ice has retreated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arctic-ocean.jpg" alt="Arctic Ocean" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CIA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arctic_Ocean_-_en.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
